:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/223"} "Henley Royal Regatta Course, Henley-on-Thames"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/158096"} "108 from 12 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "1,929 metres"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The coxed eights remained the signature event of the Olympic rowing programme, even though it was not the most popular one in terms of national participation. Since it had first been contested in " [:a {:href "/results/157523"} "1900"] ", the United States had never lost (Great Britain won in " [:a {:href "/results/157561"} "1908"] " and " [:a {:href "/results/157617"} "1912"] ", when the Americans did not submit a crew). The Americans were, therefore, the overwhelming favorites in London, where they were represented by the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/290"} "Golden Bears of UC Berkeley"] ". The only other nation that was considered as having even a remote chance at gold was Great Britain, who was represented by the " [:a {:href "/affiliations/917"} "Thames Rowing Club"] ", and whose lineup included " [:a {:href "/athletes/37282"} "Jack Dearlove"] ", who had been among the latest victors in the Grand Challenge Cup at the Henley Royal Regatta. Italy sent its reigning European Championship team, who would defend their crown for the next two years (with a slightly different lineup in 1950)."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The Americans dominated the entire competition, while Great Britain, Italy, and Canada were the other heat winners in the opening round. The width at Henley prevented more than three boats from competing at once. Thus, Italy, who had the misfortune of being placed against the United States in the semi-finals, were eliminated prior to the medal round, while Great Britain and Norway defeated Canada and Portugal, respectively, to ensure a spot on the podium. The final was no contest: the Americans won by over 10 seconds, continuing their undefeated streak, while the Britons settled for silver by finishing 3.4 seconds ahead of Norway."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/40912"} "Ian Turner"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40910"} "Dave Turner"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40689"} "Jim Hardy"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40528"} "George Ahlgren"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40571"} "Lloyd Butler"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40565"} "Dave Brown"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40878"} "Justus Smith"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40882"} "John Stack"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/40841"} "Ralph Purchase"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "Great Britain"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GBR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GBR.png"}] "GBR"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "8"} [:a {:href "/athletes/37209"} "Chris Barton"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37366"} "Michael Lapage"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37444"} "Guy Richardson"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37221"} "Paul Bircher"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37395"} "Paul Massey"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37375"} "Brian Lloyd"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37408"} "John Meyrick"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37407"} "Paul Mellows"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/37282"} "Jack Dearlove"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} "Norway"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle"